# Scope of the semgrep gate (H-22): the code that SHIPS — the library crates'
# `src/` and the `rusty_h264` CLI. Everything below is developer tooling that is
# never compiled into a published library or the CLI binary: measurement and
# A/B harnesses (`examples/`, `bench/`, `video-tests/`), scripts (`tools/`),
# test suites, and the nightly-only fuzz crate. Those programs read argv and
# write scratch files in the system temp dir BY DESIGN — that is their whole
# job — so p/rust's `args` / `temp-dir` / `current-exe` audit rules fire on
# every one of them (52 of the 64 findings when this file was added) without
# describing a reachable risk to anyone who depends on rusty_h264.
#
# Writing this file REPLACES semgrep's built-in default ignore list, so the
# defaults that matter here are repeated first.
.git/
target/
node_modules/
*.min.js

# Developer tooling, never shipped.
bench/
video-tests/
tools/
fuzz/
crates/*/examples/
crates/*/tests/
crates/*/benches/
tests/
